==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|detenir}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪˈteɪn/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-detain.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|eɪn|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# Keep (someone) from proceeding by holding them back or making claims on their attention.
# {{label|en|transitive}} To put under [[custody]].
# {{label|en|transitive}} To keep back or from; to withhold.
#* Jeremy Taylor
#*: '''Detain''' not the wages of the hireling.

